  "worked_solution": "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=11,\\,AB=2x+3,\\,BC=1-6x,\\,CD=3,\n$$\n\n  \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 11 & =(2x+3)+(1-6x)+3 \\\\ 11 & =-4x+7 \\\\ 4x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
